Review of a three year programme for cooperation on capacity building and research to be implemented by the Chr. Michelsen Institute (CMI) and the Centro de Estudos e Investigação Científica (CEIC) at the Universidade Católica de Angola (UCAN). 
The main purpose of the review is to advice the partners on opportunities to increase the relevance and effectiveness of the program.  A secondary purpose of the review is to advice on profile and management set up for the foreseen follow up phase 2011-2013. 

Scope of work
The review shall, to cover, but not necessarily be limited to the following issues. 

1.	Assess efficiency and  effectiveness, and advice on possible improvements;
2.	 Review and discuss achievements up to the time of the review
3.	Assess and discuss how impact of activities can be further strengthened through strenthened outreach activities; 
4.	Validate relevance with reference to recent economic, social and political events in Angola;
5.	 Financial sustainability; review  and discuss how CEIC-UCAN financing strategy can be strengthened both in terms of content and implementation;
6.	Human resource sustainability, review how the projects succeed in building

In the context of the upcoming elections in Uganda in 2021, the United Nations Development Programme (UNDP) has developed an integrated electoral support project titled “Strengthening Electoral Processes in Uganda (SEPU)”. The proposed project interventions will be centred on three thematic outputs: 

1) Transparency and inclusion in electoral process strengthened; 
2) Institutional capacity for the Electoral Commission (EC) and other electoral stakeholders enhanced; 
3) Peace mechanisms improved. 

The interventions will target the EC and other electoral stakeholders through both short term and long-term institutional capacity building measures, including embedded technical assistance, and also conflict mitigation measures such as multi-stakeholder dialogue and early warning mechanisms.

