Overall Goal
To contribute to the reduction of HIV transmission and mitigate the impact of AIDS on human suffering and the development of human, social and economic capital in Eritrea. 

Objectives
In order to achieve the above-stated goals, UNICEF, in collaboration with its partners, has set the following specific objectives to be achieved by the end of the year 2007. 

a) To reduce the prevalence of HIV/AIDS among young people by 25 %; 
b) To ensure the rights of 60 % of children affected by AIDS and orphans to basic services; 
c) To reduce the transmission of HIV from mother to child by 25% and mainstream the participation of men in the prevention and control of HIV/AIDS;
d) To support formative research to develop communication strategy for the intervention of Mother to child Transmission and increase and create awareness about HIV/AIDS through proper data collection, analysis and dissemination of information. 

Agr.partner: UNICEF
Impl.inst: UNICEF

