Research programme focusing on women in election and the democratic transition in Liberia

Objective 1: identify potential partners within the state and civil society for ongoing engagement around strengthening the role and participation of women in Liberia;

Objective 2: discern the attitudes of political leaders, members of civil society and the United Nations towards political participation and the October 2011 elections;

Objective 3: provide an analytical assessment on whether or not Liberia’s political environment has become more inclusive in regards to gender; 

Objective 4: provide an analytical assessment on the impact elections are likely to have on governance; and

Objective 5: provide an analytical assessment of the opportunities and challenges to women’s political participation.

