The contribution is intended for the organization of a regional conference for African states on the Convention on Cluster Munitions to be held in Pretoria, South Africa, on 25 - 26 March 2010, and its associated sponsorship programme. ISS will support the Government of South Africa in hosting such a conference and will manage a sponsorship programme. This support will include travel expenses. 

Objectives of the proposed activities include: 
•	To inform the countries of the region about the Convention on Cluster Munitions, particularly those who have not signed the Convention;
•	Maintain the political momentum and international visibility of the Convention on Cluster Munitions between the Oslo Signing Conference and the First Meeting of States Parties to be held in Laos, tentatively in November 2010;
•	Enhance understanding on the provisions of the Convention and the national steps needed for ratification and implementation;
•	Promote universalization of the Convention.

The Ministry will, in accordance with the agreement set out in the correspondence between ISS and the Royal Norwegian Embassy in Pretoria, contribute to ISS a grant within a maximum frame of NOK 1 365, 00,

