Fisheries, continued support from 2009-2013.  The immediate objective is for the Fisheries administration to have capacity and competence in the area of promoting the development and management of the fisheries and of aquaculture, in order to achieve sustainable and viable use of aquatic resources on the part of private operators and communities of fishermen and of fish farmers directly dependent on fishing and on aquaculture. 
Focus will be on:
?	Strengthening of the capacity of the Ministry of Fisheries for Formulation of Policies and Strategies;
?	Strengthening the Fisheries Management capacity for Fisheries Research, Fisheries Administration and Fish Inspection, including combating IUU Fishing (nationally and regionally);
?	Promotion of the development of the production of fisheries produce for consumption - includes subcomponents of Artisanal Fishing, Small Scale Aquaculture and Training by the Fisheries School;
?	Cross-cutting issues, sub-components of HIV/ AIDS, Good Governance, Gender and Environment.

