The CCR project will organise three two-day policy advisory group meetings, each with mostly African government representatives, policymakers, academics, and civil society actors, to assess: 

1.	Relations between South Africa and Nigeria; 


2.	South Africa in Southern Africa; 
3.	South Africa’s role on the UN Security Council between 2011 and 2012.

The Ministry is therefore pleased to support the project “Improving Community Safety: Armed Violence Reduction” in Sudan, which include the following activities in target communities:
1)	Strengthening Conflict Mitigation Mechanisms. DDG will offer to sponsor and facilitate a conference to bring together communities and key disarmament actors in order to raise awareness of potential issues and allay misconstrued concerns related to the campaign. As a follow up to this conference, DDG will facilitate the strengthening of inter-communal communication channels in conflict hotspots, and help deploy trusted local brokers to assist in conflict mitigation and resolution;
2)	Piloting Community Based Policing. Building on the success of their community based policing (CBP) in Somalia, DDG will be able to offer further training to key police personnel who can later act as trainers for other CBP staff. DDG can facilitate the setting up of CBP Community Committees and mentor both sides in order to develop trust and highlight key practical considerations of CBP in the South Sudan context, as well as preparing and implementing community-led strategies for addressing the target communities’ safe

Strengthening the Skills of the Population of Bas-Uele on Civics and Good Governance. 
The country is about to put in place democratic institutions, and legal texts exist. But, the population needs to get to know this and to be able to take advantages of it if the country shall enter a state of privilege for the people.
The project aims to inform and teach the population on how to take charge of themselves, to enjoy their rights and to know their obligations. Information and teaching will be given through seminars, workshops, radio, conferences and debates.&#65533;

Strengthening the Skills of the Population of Bas-Uele on Civics and Good Governance. 
The country is about to put in place democratic institutions, and legal texts exist. But, the population needs to get to know this and to be able to take advantages of it if the country shall enter a state of privilege for the people.
